From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glasswave <glasswave@local>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:35:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cmd, playback: reclaim headless idle memory, bound disk cache
 and cancel deleted downloads

Headless mode disables upstream periodic timers (FreeOSMemory, diskCache EvictExpired, session reaper) to stay timer-free when idle. Without replacements, freed Go heap pages from ALAC decryption remained pinned at peak RSS (~1.8-2.0 GB), the helper disk cache grew unboundedly on disk (default limit 0 / TTL 0) alongside Glasswave's own cache, and skipped tracks kept running detached background cache downloads after DELETE /api/v1/playback/{id}.

Add event-driven cooldown-guarded debug.FreeOSMemory() once headless active streams drop to zero, bound headless diskCache to a 256 MB / 1-day staging window with one-shot startup eviction, cancel in-flight headless startCacheDownload goroutines when their session is released, and lazily sweep expired sessions on Open when the background reaper is disabled.

